				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Common): Extend ProviderType enum with remaining VS Code provider types\n\nAdd the final batch of VS Code language server protocol provider types to complete alignment with upstream: InlineEdit, MappedEdits, MultiDocumentHighlight, NotebookContent, RemoteAuthorityResolver, ResourceLabelFormatter, and ScmResourceGroup.\n\nThis follows the previous commit that added DebugConfiguration, TextDocumentContent, FileSystem, UriHandler, DocumentPasteEdit, DocumentDropEdit, NotebookSerializer, TerminalProfile, TerminalLink, InlineCompletion, FileDecoration, and ExternalUriOpener. The enum now covers 51 provider types for full VS Code compatibility.",
			"SHA": "234be93fd7db2071cabc7beda8475d78c43bcf85"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T17:24:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				342,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Common): Add Git IPC channels and extend ProviderType enum\n\nAdd new IPC channel definitions for Git operations: cancel, checkout, clone, exec, fetch, isAvailable, pull, revListCount, and revParse. These channels route to Mountain subprocess handlers that invoke native git binaries.\n\nAlso extend the ProviderType enum with additional VS Code language server protocol provider types: DebugConfiguration, TextDocumentContent, FileSystem, UriHandler, DocumentPasteEdit, DocumentDropEdit, NotebookSerializer, TerminalProfile, TerminalLink, InlineCompletion, FileDecoration, and ExternalUriOpener.\n\nThese additions complete the IPC surface for Git operations and align the Common crate with VS Code's full provider type coverage.",
			"SHA": "778291ced8f9fefe781d0171720bdd91f3ec555e"
		}
	],
